{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1381567-my-homebrew-2ed-kiths","id":1381567,"title":"My Homebrew 2ed Kiths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-15T01:46:26-07:00","id":1381567,"title":"My Homebrew 2ed Kiths","content":"I only have one right now, but I'll post more in this thread as I write them.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Caretaker </b></i></u><br /> <i>&quot;The sick of spirit are still people, but some need more help than others.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Some Gentry occasionally realize that others perceive them as being absolutely mad, and start to wonder what is this whole idea of madness that mortals keep associating with them. Those Gentry who do not dismiss the concept outright (because they're perfect beings, naturally) find it amusing to play up their status as being unsound of mind and in need of a psychologist. Changelings of this Kith were forced to listen for years on end to alien and horrid thought processes and try to make sense of them, but there is no curing the Gentry of their capricious solipsism. This type of Durance allows Caretakers to heal mental ailments and understand others more reliably, but they often display ironically (or maybe fittingly) neurotic behaviors as a result of such intimacy with their Keepers.<ul><li><b>Beast:</b> Therapy dogs and cats with a lot of love to give. Brightly colored songbirds that inspire and motivate. Monkeys that make you laugh with their quirky sense of humor.</li> <li><b>Fairest:</b> \u200bTheirs is a subtle Mien indeed. They usually aren't beautiful in a physical sense, but they emanate a luminous aura of understanding and compassion like a sort of halo.</li> <li><b>Ogre:</b> They won't be coddling your ego, and will make it a point to help you grow a skin that is just as stone-like as theirs.</li> </ul><b>Kith Blessing:</b> When the Caretaker uses Empathy to understand and treat psychological ailments in general, he receives Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Voice Of Reason:</b> The Changeling may spend a point of Glamour and roll Wits + Empathy once per day per patient to either let them automatically experience a Dramatic Failure on their next roll for a Clarity Breaking Point, or give them the Rote Quality on their next Integrity Breaking Point. This takes the form of a therapy session which lasts one hour per patient, but the particulars are up to the Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-15-2020, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T06:49:49-07:00","id":1381906,"title":"","content":"Ooo! Subtle, but I like it. Mad-house sanitarium-realm in Arcadia, where changelings are forced to live out a Bedlam Hospital-style controlled chaos all. The. Time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T18:47:44-08:00","id":1472339,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>Phantasm</b></i></u><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What's the matter, scared of that howling? We better take a different Trod, follow me.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Not every Changeling is given an important, fixed role in Arcadia. Some are transformed into mercurial and protean forms in order to act as living illusions. Some Gentry use these captives as luring mechanisms in order to prevent others from escaping. Other Gentry populate entire opera theaters or movie studios with them in order to present macabre shows for others of their capricious kind. Many people who end up as Phantasms had some talent for entertainment or deceit before the Durance. After returning to the Ironside, their penchant for illusion often leads them into pursuing lifestyles which facilitate a certain flair for the dramatic and performative, regardless of veracity.<ul><li><b>Beast:</b> \u200bA chameleon whose scales reflect light in a way that generates colorful holograms.</li> <li><b>Elemental:</b> An entity made of several fragment of stained glass, with a perfectly spherical prism for a head.\u200b</li> <li><b>Wizened:</b> A living puppet with ornate mechanical joints, and eyes made of projectors or lanterns.</li> </ul><b>Kith Blessing:</b> When making Expression rolls to entrance, distract or entertain people, achieve Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> <br /> <b>More Real Than Reality:</b> The Changeling may spend 1 Glamour and roll Manipulation + Expression + Wyrd vs Wits + Supernatural Advantage in order to create an illusion within his direct line of sight, which lasts for the scene but can be cancelled at will. This affects one of the five senses per Success, but is considered to affect everyone rather than only existing inside the mind of one person. This illusion does not possess its own will, and thus only acts out what the Changeling imagined, no more and no less. <br /> <br /> By also taking 1 point of Severe Clarity Damage, the illusion counts as an automaton which will follow a complex command, which is to phrased as a single sentence. If need be, the illusion counts as Retainer with a Rating equal to Successes, up to 5. The Changeling can only have a maximum number of illusions active simultaneously equal to his Wyrd. Of note is that the illusion cannot affect anything physically, only convince people that it does. Characters with an ability to pierce supernatural deceit initiate a Clash Of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T08:24:38-08:00","id":1472362,"title":"","content":"Is this thread just for your own kiths r should I link in the ones from Homebrew Kiths 2: Goblin Bugaboos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T08:54:23-08:00","id":1472363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1381567-my-homebrew-2ed-kiths?p=1472362#post1472362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this thread just for your own kiths r should I link in the ones from Homebrew Kiths 2: Goblin Bugaboos</div> </div> </div> </div> Go ahead and cross-post if you want.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T11:36:41-08:00","id":1472378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1381567-my-homebrew-2ed-kiths?p=1472363#post1472363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Go ahead and cross-post if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> wait, would crossposting be just posting the link, or copy-pasting the full text?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T11:48:16-08:00","id":1472379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1381567-my-homebrew-2ed-kiths?p=1472378#post1472378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait, would crossposting be just posting the link, or copy-pasting the full text?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can copy-paste the full text, as far as I know.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T14:58:03-08:00","id":1472386,"title":"","content":"<b>Brownie</b><br /> <br /> <i>No, I don't need a spotter. Trust me, all hands are on deck here.</i><br /> <br /> If anyone would envy the position of all but the lowliest Chatelaines, it would be the Busybodies. If the Chatelaine is the fancy butler or maid with their own title, waiting on a great Lord of the Fae, then the Brownie us the local Gentry squire\u2019s soap-scarred housekeeper. Brownies are made by those Gentry who, for one reason or another, want a servant and can\u2019t keep more than a few at once. But even the lowest Gentry are proud, and will live with no less than the full package of servile services. They pick dull workaholics and stretch them out, to create a servant that can do the work of an entire staff. Punishment for failure is swift, but many have escaped when they realized that they ran so much of the Domain that it bowed to their whim.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental</b>: She is a swirling mass of mud that defaults to a vaguely humanoid shape, but when pressed, she shapes out new appendages as needed.<br /> <b>Darkling</b>: her four compound eyes flit around the room at dizzying speeds, translating and performing the dark ritual in real time<br /> <b>Wizened</b>: A thin bent house elf, with a steampunk backpack grafted to their spine full of extra appendages<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: When rolling to perform standard household chores, from cleaning to baking, three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <b>Inhuman Industry</b>: By spending 1 glamour and meditating for a full minute, a Brownie can temporarily split their mind. This allows them to perform at least two extended actions with similar roll intervals at the same time. They can take a -1 penalty to all affected actions to add another extended action to the same roll interval, or multiply that penalty by two for each extended action beyond the third. The effect lasts until the Changeling finishes or fails each of the Extended Tests she started when she invoked this power, or when she puts them down and leaves them unfinished for a time to do something else in the interim.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1470389-homebrew-kiths-2-goblin-bugaboos\">Here </a>is the thread with the kiths from other homebrewers also.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> This split off from an initial idea for a kith built around extra limbs that got fleshed out too far for one thing. I've also been trying to do a grapple kith, as a Blessing for melee grapples was a neat blessing I thought. So far, I'm still trying to figure out how to either make grappling semi-viable in the face of Portalling, or how to make using it on non-Changelings only still feel cool.<br /> <br /> If there's a way to make grappling viable without just giving them the power to nullify Portalling, I'll make a wrestler kith.<br /> <br /> But the idea that appeals to me is taking inspiration from Rodeo Riders, Tarzan and Crocodile Dundee and focus them on taming animals through brute strength and charisma, to use them as tools and partners in later scrapes. I just need to find a good Trickery. Here's my first few ideas:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>A calming song that works on both people and animals until you make any move to tie them up or hurt them</li> <li>Some sort of calming musk scent that does something similar to the song</li> <li>Roll something to add successes in either Structure or Durability to any rope or chain you hold</li> <li>Something to either speed up how long it takes to get the Bonded Condition with an animal, or just grant it temporarily</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":".  reworking Brownie 01-15-2022, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T11:04:28-08:00","id":1472459,"title":"","content":"<b>Spinster</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Seen me in your dreams? You\u2019d be surprised at how often I hear that.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Some Gentry cloak themselves in fragments of dreams wonder, stolen from a mortal. But sometimes the Others take a fancy for those who dreams they stalk. Spinsters are made from those who lived in their dreams. Many find themselves trapped in a new dream, that they can\u2019t seem to wake up from. Some were assigned to guard and mislead any who would seek a Huntsman's Heart. Some instead helped assist their Keeper steal bits of dreams, and help make the Baubles. Some even wandered their Keepers dreams, looking for any exit. Spinsters have lived a ever shifting landscape of horrors and wonders. Even when they return, many are still more comfortable in dreams than the waking world.<br /> <br /> Darkling: A hunch and shriveled thing that seems to remind you of sleep paralysis.<br /> Elemental: She is a swarm of bubbles, all pressed into the shape of a person, each containing a differing scene and emotion.<br /> Ogre: He reminds you of an oversized pushed toy, big, soft, and comforting.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing</b>: When rolling Empathy to understand someone whose dreams they have seen, three successes counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Sweet Dreams: By spending 3 glamour when gaining a Dream Condition, a Spinster may reduce the penalties of a Condition representing a Dreams hostility to its Preceding Condition\u2019s level. This doesn\u2019t extend to reduction of impression for Social Maneuvering, nor prevent non hostile failures from being upgraded to dramatic failures. By spending 1 glamour, a Spinster can reduce the penalties towards a dreamweaving action by half of their Wyrd.<br /> <br /> As for the wrestler kith, actually keeping a hold on a Changeling isn\u2019t actually very interesting to me. It\u2019s good for a huntsman, just not really granting you a new and interesting way to approach problems. I\u2019ve been trying to make a constrictor snake person forever, so my first thought for a kith would be to replicate something that grappling animals can do. Like Spiders, Snakes and Squid, I think. Looking at your other possible trickeries, the adding Structure or Durability to chain or rope actually is pretty cool, I can actually see lots of different characters desiring and using that. If you absolutely need holding down a Changeling as the power, I recommend this one to pair it with. Maybe pair it with the Chain or Lasso weapons and Might of the Terrible Brute for a rather unusual, but effective fighter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}